<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Algeria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Algeria is a country in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. Its territory formed part of medieval empires such as the Almoravid domains and was later an Ottoman province governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> conquered it from 1830, making it the most important settler colony of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>, until independence in 1962.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/algeria.jpg" alt="Algeria" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: National Liberation Front of Algeria Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Algeria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
